Following rumors about C3 Presents creating a new music festival in Philadelphia, the promoter/producer announced the Vineland Music Festival in New Jersey, in partnership with Festival Republic of British producer Melvin Benn.
“For our company, it is an honour to work with a person who, no more and no less, inspired the current festival movement in America,” Charlie Jones of C3 told Billboard.com.
C3 produced the Lollapalooza festival of Chicago and the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Vineland in New Jersey is a summer camping destination.
The festival is scheduled to be held from 8 to 10 August on a 500-a-a-a-half-a-half-a-half-a-500-a-half-of-500-a-500-a-500-a-500-a-500-
Previously known as Mean Fiddler, the director of Festival Republic, Melvin Benn, is one of the most respected festival producers in the world.
In 1989 he took the helm of the Reading Festival in the United Kingdom, which annually attracted some 80,000 people.
In 1999, Melvin Benn added the Leeds Festival to its portfolio, then in 2006, Festival Republic premiered Henham Park's Latitude Festival in Suffolk.
Since 2002, as co-poe owner, Melvin Benn is also in charge of Glastonbury Festival production, licensing and organizational tasks, which can now accommodate up to 177,500 people.
Calling Glastonbury the "most inspiring event" he has ever attended, Charlie Jones de C3 says his company and Melvin Benn work in parallel to give the region a European-style festival-event.
“We chose Philadelphia as the market and worked assiduously with the Fairmount Parks Commission to create a festival in downtown Philadelphia,” says Jones.
“We were in talks with the city and the Commission was motivated and excited about this project.
Sadly, we got bogged down in politicians because of the current administration.
“Happily, we were able to talk to Melvin Benn and we are preparing to create a beautiful festival on an exceptional site that will ultimately serve the people of Philadelphia.”
C3 Presents resurrected the Lollapalooza festival in 2005 at the Grant Park in Chicago, dissociating in the festival landscape in 2002 with the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
The two events had a gross revenue of Euro9.8 million and Euro11.1 million in 2007.
These two festivals are held in an urban setting.
'Melvin Benn's European model is a rural-fashioned festival, while ours rather take place in urban green spaces,' says Charlie Jones.
The objective is to merge, in one way or in some way, the two formulas to give an impression of both European and American-style rural festivals.'
Vineland is about halfway between Philadelphia and Atlantic City.
'The community of Vineland, including the mayor, enthusiastically supports the holding of this event,' says Charlie Jones.
The latter refuses to reveal the terms of the agreement, but says 'they are interesting enough to make it possible to invest in such an event and to host a festival which hopefully will have a long life.'
Charlie Jones stated that the hospitality of this festival is "very great", as is the ability of 80,000 people from Bonnaroo Music Festival at Tennessee.
He said that invitations had been issued to the groups, but that nothing could yet be confirmed at the time of printing.
'Vineland will be rock-flavoured, but the music will be varied, in the hope of locating all kinds of spectators,' says Charlie Jones.
Its partners in C3, who received the Top Independent Promoter Award from the last Billboard Touring Awards, were Charlie Walker and Charles Attal.
