The Banque Populaire will open 200 offices open from 12 p.m. from Monday to Saturday
Banque Populaire has decided to renovate a large part of its offices.
A total of 200 are banks located in the most commercial areas of Spain.
These branches, which will operate under the Popular Max brand, represent a major change for the bank.
Also for the rest of the Spanish bodies, since it is the first group that decided to start to betting on the uninterrupted opening of its agencies until 8.30 p.m., and to open on Saturday from 10 a.m. to 8.30 p.m.
Another group which has also repeatedly reiterated that it wishes to amplify the schedules of its branches, BBVA, although it has not yet decided to take the first step.
It is in the verge of concluding an agreement with the trade unions to close 75 per cent of its agencies on Saturdays instead of opening an afternoon, but not for the public.
The results of People's Bank experience will be a key step towards whether or not other agencies are a member of this initiative, which coincides with business schedules.
It is precisely this objective that the People’s Bank is looking for.
Attract self-driving customers in these areas to shop in SMEs and street shops chosen to open.
The bank wants to open these 200 branches located throughout Spain in about 18 months, since it is not a question of the opening of new agencies but of a renovation of existing ones.
To this end, the organization will modernise the branches it already has in commercial areas, adapting them to the profile of the customers of the different streets.
In this way, the amplification of timetables is accompanied by a different design of the interior of the branch and a new, more up-to-date design with brighter colors.
The sales manager, Angel Rivera, assures that this renovation does not involve major investments, but the hiring of staff, since the employee number will be increased from six to eight or nine per agency.
The agencies, which will also have space so that SMEs can meet there, will sell non-financial products.
A positive experience for the group
The Banque Populaire has already tested its initiative in three agencies in Madrid.
And the experiment has been positive, as Angel Rivero explains.
Branches of Murillo Brave, O'Donnell Street and the Gran Via of Madrid are the streets to be chosen, and apparently successfully, according to Rivero.
Banque Populaire currently owns 2,500 branches.
And there are a number of others operating under the Mundocredit brand, specialising in the case of Immigrants, also with very ample schedules, which open even on Sundays and on public holidays.
In these PopularMax branches they will not copy the BBVA model, where several of its agencies have a wide range of non-financial products for sale.
'We don't want to compete with our customers , notes Rivero.
For the time being, they have reached an agreement with Telefonica to sell mobile phones, with staff external to the bank.
