Mayor and Totana Local Police Chief Arrested for an All-Excited Urban Brig.
The Spanish Gendarmerie arrested the Mayor of the Murcian town of Totana, "popular" José Martinez Andreo, the head of the local police, the secretary of the town hall and a suspicious hotel entrepreneur for possible urban crimes, today informed the sources of the investigation.
The city councillor was arrested at his home and was taken to the town hall, where a large number of staff gathered, who also presented themselves to the Office of Municipal Town Planning Councillor and to the municipal company for the Management of Industrial Soil and Accommodation.
These three judgments are in addition to the six stops made last Monday in the provinces of Galicia, La Murcia and Madrid in an operation relating to the recharacterization of more than 2 million hectares of agricultural land in order for the Galician company Nuaria to build 4,000 housing units, after the payment of illegal commissions during the last legislature.
In addition, two other persons have not been summoned but are attributed in the judicial investigation, which is investigated by Totana Court No. 3.
The first six denunciations now moved to a judicial provision.
According to the sources, the previous Totana municipal councillor and currently an autonomous parliamentary of the PP party, Juan Morales, is covered by the investigation.
In addition, the ex-wiwife, owner of a real estate agency currently registered in Totana, was imputed, as well as the current fiancée of the former city councillor residing in Murcia.
The director and owner of the Nuaria Group, the lawyer and entrepreneur of Vigo (Galice), Manuel N.A., were arrested in Nigrun (Pontevedra), as well as Pablo José M.G, Director of Suelo de Inmonuar, an agency of the Nuaria Group, through which the bribes would have been produced.
The investigation is the responsibility of the Urban Crimes Group of the Central Operative Unit (UCO) of the Gendarmerie, whose agents, in addition to the stops have carried out 11 inspections, the vast majority in companies linked to detainees and located in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontevedra, Las Rozas (Madrid) and Totana.
As a result, only one person was arrested in Totana, the owner of a well-recognized poultry company in the region, which may have acted as an intermediary.
The Nuaria Group was responsible for the development of the largest residential complex in the Murcian commune of Totana, which would involve the construction of more than 5,000 dwellings, a golf course and two "spa".
In Totan, the company acquired 2.2 million square metres of land recharacterized and its project would involve doubling the population of the commune, which currently has a population of 25,000.
The Nuaria Group consists of companies such as Autesa and Inomonuar, which deal with real estate development; Conycase, which manages car parks of Vigo in the streets of Coru'a, Venezuela and the Place de Fernando el Catailico; Hogartel, which handles direct marketing; Preconiza, which focuses on the promotion, sale and installation of building elements.
