My treating doctor told me about one of his articles about strange research entitled: 'Money produces cerebral activations, especially if the others receive less '
In other words, the feelings generated by workers' monthly payments depends on what colleagues are earning.
The study was carried out with tomographic magnetic resonances at the University of Bonn, and the results are published in the latest issue of Science.
According to Bernd Weber, author of the study and director of the neurocognition Image group at the Life-Brain Institute in Germany: 'The biggest activation occurred when the participant responded correctly and his companion failed.
The researchers observed that when the two people guessed that they received the same pay, the activation was moderate, but if one of them received twice, the activation was greater.
