20,000 people attend in Vancouver in the first concert of the Spice Girls tour
The Spice Girls initiated in Vancouver (Canada), facing about 20,000 spectators, their first tour since the band dissipated in 2000.
'Posh Spice ' (Victoria Beckham), ' Scary Spice' (Melanie Brown), ' Baby Spice' (Emma Bunton), 'Sporty Spice' (Melanie Chisholm) and Ginger Spice (Geri Halliwell) stated shortly before commencing their gontification at Vancouver's GM Stadium
Around 20,000 people have exhausted tickets to attend the concert which was the subject of a video in which the story of the band that was enraged at the end of 1990.
The game and world tour coincided with the launch of a new album resuming their main successes as well as two new songs, "Headlines" and "Voodoo", which EMI published in Spain.
Spice Girl's five members took to the stage by showing the bracelets that "Posh Spice's bridegroom gave them, British Footballer David Beckham).
The athlete was in the audience filling the GM Place, even though Victoria forbade it a few days earlier.
Prior to the start of the show, Victoria Beckham remarked that the British Footballer "didn't see our costume but I'm nervous because I don't know what he's going to think about the show".
'Sporty Spice' which left the group in 1998 "because of the differences between us" and which led to the dissolving of the group two years later, also expressed its nervousness during an interview with the press, two hours before the start of the show.
"I was scared.
I was nervous, but I've seen that people's feeling has changed, the feeling for the Spice Girls has changed.
And I've been wondering why not, I'm happy to have made a decision," Chisholm said of the group meeting she disbanded nine years ago.
The singer also remarked over time, "threats have been arranged and we greatly appreciate ourselves".
But a great deal has changed since the Spice Girl exhibited for the last time in 1998.
For starters, according to CTV television, the group arrived in Vancouver on a special Virgin Airlines plane.
