Von Beust received criticism for the cancellation of the Olympiad.
The mayor's re-entry from the Hamburg candidacy for the Summer Olympic Summer Olympics collided with virulent critics in politics and the economy.
Many people want to continue to fight for the Waterfront Games.
But Von Beust calls for realism in assessing opportunities.
The senior director of the Chamber of Commerce in Hamburg, Hans-Jurg Schmidt-Trenz, described on Wednesday an abandonment as "wrong for the local economy".
In recent times, no other project had deployed as many motivating forces in the city as the Olympiad idea.
"Without this objective, the political-sporting momentum could not have been maintained in the same measures".
Schmidt-Trenz invited the Senate not to bury the project, but to find it a new longer-term starting point, "taking another modified agenda as its starting point".
May Mayor Ole von Beust stayed on Wednesday for his previous statements, according to which Hamburg's Olympic ambitions were at least unrealistic until the year 2028.
'It is not Hamburg to decide on a candidacy for the Olympiads, but the German Olympic Sports Federation,' Von Beust told WELT ONLINE.
It refers to the expected decision of the Sports Federation in early December, on the Munich candidacy for Winter Play in 2018.
This preference means for us that, in the lapse of time we had planned until 2028 until then, we will have no luck."
But the dream doesn't definitely belong to the past, said Von Beust.
The Hamburg Sports Federation (HSB) regretted Beust's statements.
The impression would be that Hamburg would no longer want to apply for the Olympic Games over the next 25 years.
'It is too early to close an opportunity, burying the plans already now,' said HSB President Gunter Ploi on Wednesday.
An abandonment of the candidacy would no longer be at odds with the statements made by the head of the Senate on the occasion of the reception in plenary meeting of the German Federation of Higher Schools of Sport.
There, Von Beust would have qualified Hamburg's candidacy for the 2015 Universiades as "not a substitute" for the Olympic Games in Hamburg.
The Federation of Superior Schools of Sport had in the past weeks first appointed Hamburg as a candidate city.
The mayor's SPD fraction blamed the Senate for not having used this precious time in the construction of housing in Hamburg.
"Little Grasbrook development was rejected by the Senate for years because it played the Olympiad map and excluded the construction of housing," SPD delegates Carola Veit and Jan Quast said.
While the SPD has always called for Little Grasbrook a plan built into the Olympiads and a subsequent use of housing, the CDU would have relied exclusively on the "Factor Event".
Candidacy for the 2012 Summer Summer Olympics would have sparked a lot of excitement in Hamburg.
However, Hamburg had smashed itself against Leipzig.
It wasn't Warhols.
The one that connects the concepts Sweden and a wooden box, thinks about Ikea, but not Andy Warhol.
Or so?
At the moment, wooden crates manufactured in Sweden cast shades on Warhol's list of works.
A large proportion of "Type ThorStatpose" Brillo-Boxes listed there are forgeries.
After a few months a few months ago questioned the authenticity of Andy Warhol's Brillo-Box of the year 1968, the in-house research of the Moderna Museet in Stockholm now leads to a disenunciable result: the six "Brillo-Boxes", of which the former director of the Pontus Hulten Museum made a gift in 1995 to the Moderna Museet
Ancient history is entangled, disconceiving with artistic and curatorical productions.
In 1964, Warhol created in New-York its first "Brillo-Boxes", painted wooden bundles, which are based on the red-blue-blue-white design of "Brillo" soap cardboard.
Exhibition of his work at the Moderna Museet presented in 1968 - with the Warhol agreement - hundreds of Brillo clamps made of cardboard: These did not come (for financial reasons) from Warhol, but had been delivered directly from the Brillo cardboard factory.
These were not works of works of art, but rather their models, exposure samples.
At the same time, Warhol made permission in 1968 to produce a few Brillo bundles in Sweden which were not on display in the Moderna Museet.
Testimonies at the time today speak of about fifteen wooden hustles which at the time entered law into the history of the art and auctions, as original Brillo-Boxes of Authorized Andy Warhol, with the name "Type Stockholm".
Some of them reached more than USD 100,000 in auctions.
The problem now is that the legendary Pontus Hultén museum's legendary director immediately claimed that about a hundred wooden bundles had been produced and exhibited in Sweden in 1968 that Warhol would subsequently have ceded.
In fact, Hultén's 105 coffers were produced in Malmo in 1990 for an Exhibition in St-Fetersburg.
By that time, Warhol had already been dead for three years.
The chief curator of the Moderna Museet, the chief curator of the Moderna Museet, examined, next to the six Brillo-Boxes in the museum, three other of Swedish private collectors, of which two were prepared in Stockholm in 1968: their laminate panels were first printed and swollen, followed by a brush in white oil.
The texture of copies dating back to the year 1990 reveals, on the other hand, that the paint was applied directly without a background layer to the laminate panels, using a scroll of paint - in addition, it is not an oil-paint, an accrylic.
"These crates have not been authorized by the artist and should be removed from Andy Warhol's official Brillo-Boxes list," suggests the Director of Moderna Museet, Lars Nittve: 'While the 'Andy Warhol Art Authentication Board in New-York doesn't come another decision, the Moderna Museet will classify all six boxes in its collection.
Already in July the Authentication Board has, of course, announced that it would investigate the "heavy charges" that will be raised in the case of boxes of soap powder.
But we've been amazed there with an inexorable silence.
Manila Relative Soldiers Leave
In the Philippines, the rebel soldiers were abandoning, the same ones who had entrenched themselves in a hotel in Manila, and who had demanded the withdrawal of President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo.
Chief Antonio Trillanes, reproducing corruption and electoral idlapsing by the President, told reporters in the hotel that he could not answer for any blunderstrapping.
Soldiers loyal to the authorities immediately stormed the hotel using tear gas.
Twenty-two-dozen soldiers had been captivating for hours in the building.
About half of them stood before the courts on Wednesday due to an attempted failed coup in 2003 – including Trillanes.
He took advantage of the audience to eclipse suddenly with about 30 sympathizers.
The military police, who were to normally monitor them, had apparently deserted on his behalf and joined his mutiny.
They introduced themselves into the Peninsula Hotel and forced President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo to withdraw.
Trounts loyal to the authorities closed the area around the respectable hotel.
The president convened an urgent meeting of the Security Cabinet.
National Security Adviser Norberto Gonzales condemned the actions of the soldiers.
'People have enough,' said Trillanes.
'We call on people to join us.'
General Danilo Lim, who commanded Scout Ranger Elect Unit before, stated that other army units soon wanted to join the march.
Criticism of the regime called for a major demonstration against the President on Wednesday.
His Government had been overwhelmed by reproach of corruption for months.
Manila's financial district had already been the scene of the attempted mutiny of about 200 army members against Arroyo since 2003.
The uprising shackled almost 24 hours after the army's refusal to join.
Since 1986 there have already been at least seven coup attempts against democratically elected governments in the Philippines.
United Internet became a principal shareholder of Versatel.
United Internet secured more than 20 per cent of the telecommunications company Versatel.
The average price per share is EUR 14.46, as communicated by the company on Wednesday.
Only 20.05 per cent of the share capital would be owned.
A buy-back had been spawned earlier.
The option would remain open to further increase participation in Versatel.
This step is seeking to speed up the consolidation of the German DSL market, the United Internet reported.
Just in the past, suppositions had already been made on an entry on Wednesday, after Berenberg Bank had increased its participation in the Dusseldorf network operator from 5 per cent to 15.1 per cent.
The credit institution would hold the money only for a third part, it says on the market.
The day before, United Internet had already acquired nearly 10 per cent stake in the mobile phone company Drillisch.
As part of a capital increase, Drillisch invested 17.4 million new equities worth EUR 106.4 million.
United Internet purchased EUR 5.15 million for EUR 31.1 million.
In addition, companies have opened negotiations on cooperation in the commercialisation of DSL and mobile products.
"We are strengthening our partnership," a spokeswoman for the United Internet
The two companies founded the MSP shareholding company in order to absorb the competitor Freenet.
For the time being, the two companies want to feel satisfied with their ten per cent stake at Freenet, and do not make use of an additional 18.49 per cent of Freenet, United Internet said on Thursday.
However, the two companies would allow themselves all the open options, in particular to increase the shareholding in SA Freenet, it was learned.
Negotiations between United Internet and Freenet on a strategic partnership had ended in mid-October.
Poker still difficult to predict on Freenet which has lasted for months is part of the consolidation of the German telecoms market.
By the end of the third quarter, Freenet had 2.9 million customers bound by a mobile telephony contract and 1.27 million DSL and full-subscribing customers.
The Holding of United Internet and Drillisch previously had a 7.0 per cent direct stake in Freenet.
It has now been agreed that Drillisch will provide about an additional 4 per cent.
The right to purchase 18.49 per cent of the investment company Vatas had already been decided in August.
